    },
    {
      "title": "Reds @ Jays Game Thread",
      "summary": "Game 161. Are there any other sports that play 162 games in a season? Can you imagine if MLB played just 17 games a season? It would be a whole different spot. So, I had a night last night. Men\u2019s Night Out, a charity thing for my wife\u2019s church. I\u2019m the least religious person you\u2019ll [&#8230;]",
      "source": "Bluebird Banter",
      "author": "tom dakers",
      "url": "https://www.bluebirdbanter.com/toronto-blue-jays-gamethreads/63945/reds-jays-game-thread",
      "published": "2026-09-26T18:52:44+00:00"
    },
    {
      "title": "Saturday Jays Notes",
      "summary": "Second-to-last day of the regular season. There isn\u2019t much news. Max Scherzer says he\u2019ll wait until after the season to decide whether he wants to pitch next year, but he&#8217;s set to start tomorrow, in front of his kids (just in case). He hasn\u2019t put up numbers that would make me want to re-sign him. [&#8230;]",
      "source": "Bluebird Banter",
      "author": "tom dakers",
      "url": "https://www.bluebirdbanter.com/news/63942/saturday-jays-notes",
      "published": "2026-09-26T17:21:18+00:00"
    },
    {
      "title": "Jays Edge Reds 6-5",
      "summary": "For most of the night, this looked like a typically frustrating 2026 Blue Jays loss. The starting pitching wasn\u2019t very good, the bullpen did enough to keep them in range, and while the offence produce traffic on the bases it failed to turn that into runs. Luckily, things flipped late. The offence woke up and [&#8230;]",
      "source": "Bluebird Banter",
      "author": "Tom Mullie",
      "url": "https://www.bluebirdbanter.com/toronto-blue-jays-scores/63936/jays-edge-reds-6-5",
      "published": "2026-09-26T02:44:43+00:00"
    },
    {
      "title": "Reds @ Jays Game Thread",
      "summary": "Game One of the last series of the season. Not surprisingly, there was a roster move: CJ Van Eyk was optioned to Buffalo and John Klein has been recalled. So we only have two more days of roster moves let. And Vlad apologized for his comment. People that are mad about it all aren\u2019t going [&#8230;]",
      "source": "Bluebird Banter",
      "author": "tom dakers",
      "url": "https://www.bluebirdbanter.com/toronto-blue-jays-gamethreads/63928/reds-jays-game-thread",
      "published": "2026-09-25T22:31:30+00:00"
    },
    {
      "title": "Jays/Reds Series Preview",
      "summary": "The last series of the season and there is no playoff implications. Likely starting pitchers: The Reds are 74-85, last in the NL Central (Jays are 77-82, last in the AL East). The Reds have scored 4.12 runs per game, last in the NL (the Jays are last in the AL in runs per game [&#8230;]",
      "source": "Bluebird Banter",
      "author": "tom dakers",
      "url": "https://www.bluebirdbanter.com/news/63923/jays-reds-series-preview",
      "published": "2026-09-25T16:48:30+00:00"
    },
    {
      "title": "Today In Jays History: Delgado Hits Four Home Runs",
      "summary": "23 Years Ago Moments like these always make me feel old\u2014I never would have guessed this happened so long ago. Carlos Delgado hit four home runs against the Tampa Bay Devil Rays (before they changed their name). This rare feat has occurred only six times in American League history and just 18 times in MLB [&#8230;]",
      "source": "Bluebird Banter",
      "author": "tom dakers",
      "url": "https://www.bluebirdbanter.com/blue-jay-history/63911/today-in-jays-history-delgado-hits-four-home-runs",
      "published": "2026-09-25T12:52:00+00:00"
    },
    {
      "title": "Off-Day Open Thread",
      "summary": "It is the last off-day of the regular season, before the series with the Reds. I forgot that today was an off-day. I went to see what time tonight\u2019s game was starting and whoops there isn\u2019t a tonight\u2019s game. And there isn\u2019t much for Jays news. Everything is about Vlad\u2019s interview, and I think I [&#8230;]",
      "source": "Bluebird Banter",
      "author": "tom dakers",
      "url": "https://www.bluebirdbanter.com/general/63919/off-day-open-thread",
      "published": "2026-09-24T19:26:57+00:00"
    },
    {
      "title": "Happy Birthday John McDonald",
      "summary": "John McDonald celebrates his 52nd birthday today. John McDonald enjoyed a remarkable career, especially for someone with a lifetime .233/.273/.323 slash line. How does a player last 16 years in the majors with numbers like that? The answer: exceptional defensive ability. Several years ago, I asked Brian Butterfield about Mac. Last year in Seattle, we [&#8230;]",
      "source": "Bluebird Banter",
      "author": "tom dakers",
      "url": "https://www.bluebirdbanter.com/blue-jay-history/63914/happy-birthday-john-mcdonald",
      "published": "2026-09-24T15:38:47+00:00"
    },
    {
      "title": "Jays Lose Game Two Of The Doubleheader",
      "summary": "Blue Jays 2 Orioles 4 Well, that was about right. Couldn\u2019t hit at all. Well, not at all, Davis Schneider hit a home run in the ninth. We did load the bases in the seventh in perhaps the weirdest way ever: We had 5 hits. Lukes had 2 of them. We also had 9 strikeouts. [&#8230;]",
      "source": "Bluebird Banter",
